    "title": "Multiple people shot at Grafton home Wednesday night - NewsBreak",
    "text": "GRAFTON — Multiple people were shot in an incident Wednesday night in which a suspect was taken into custody following a short standoff with police. State Police released initial information about the incident, but would not reveal the number of victims, or their conditions, according to spokeswoman Stephanie O'Neil. Police were called to an address on County Route 85, South Road, at about 6:40 p.m. Wednesday for a report of shots fired. When arriving, a person exited the house with a firearm. Police said \"after a brief standoff that individual was taken into custody. A search in and around the residence revealed multiple individuals with gunshot wounds.\" Grafton Supervisor Ingrid Gundrum called the news of the incident a \"tragedy,\" and said it involved a long-time family in town. South Road was closed Wednesday night between Johnson and Synder roads. Rensselaer County Sheriff Kyle Bourgault said deputies are assisting State Police. Police said a media event will likely be held Thursday to provide more information on the case. Sign up for Times Union newsletters here Read the original article on timesunion.com",
